#1502
"The Nave - South End"
"Overturned and burned benches are scattered about the south end of the nave,

the remnant of some catastrophe which befell this cathedral.  The once-proud

windows of stained glass stand broken, only gritty fragments of colour remain,

still clinging to the charred window frames.  The cathedral ceiling rises high

overhead, where an intricately-fashioned ceiling is supported by a series of

sturdy wooden arches, still standing firm despite bearing several gashes and

holes.  A pair of ruined gates lead out of the cathedral to the south, while

to the north, the nape continues.

"
"ravaged by fire

extras

search benches, etc

"
