#1503
"The Nave - North End"
"This is the north end of the nave of a once-spectacular cathedral.  Flying

arches support an ornate ceiling, scorched by fire but not completely

destroyed.  Dominating the view from the nave is the spectacular archway to

the north, a massive scissor arch which gives entrance to the altar.  To the

south, the nave continues through a maze of broken benches and shattered glass.

"
"scissor arch to n enters the altar

ravaged by fire

extras

"
